Goal: Retrieve the flag from /root/flag.txt via an unsanitized file upload.
🔍 Vulnerability Analysis
The challenge presents a file upload feature intended for profile pictures. The critical flaw is the lack of input sanitization on the uploaded file.

Vulnerability: Unrestricted File Upload (leading to Remote Code Execution).
Vector: The server accepts .php files (or executes PHP content) without validating the file extension or content type.
Impact: An attacker can upload a malicious PHP script (webshell) to execute arbitrary commands on the server.
🛠️ Exploitation Steps
1. Identify the Upload Endpoint
Accessed the web application at http://standard-pizzas.picoctf.net:56773.
Located the file upload form (likely a POST request to /upload.php).
2. Craft the Webshell
Created a simple PHP reverse shell or command execution script (shell.php):

