Note: For this challenge, a simple system() call was sufficient to execute commands.

3. Upload the Malicious File
Uploaded shell.php directly to the server.
Observation: The server accepted the file and saved it to /uploads/shell.php.
Bypass: No extension filtering or MIME type validation was enforced.
